commit 63c28785599e86c2cab4aacf9e030d0253ebbc0c

C03: who or what a named thing is gets looked up in public pages and answered from a snippet (KNOWLEDGE1473)

KNOWLEDGE1353/1355 measured that «¿Quién es Daredevil?», «Que es doom eternal=» and «Hablame un poco de Marvel vs. Capcom.» invented creators, studios, years and protagonists: the local model's memory, with no source of facts in the product. Probes from this PC show the public engine returns the pages (Wikipedia, Steam, IMDb) for the bare name and unrelated pages for the whole question. Mind: `_entity_lookup_query` reads who/what a named thing is (no article, not the assistant or the person, not a possessed or pointed thing, not a word's meaning, no question folded into the name) as a public lookup; the web.search query is the bare name; the composer instructs the answer to repeat what a snippet states about the name, in its words, naming the page, without creators, studios, dates or figures no snippet contains and without a trailing question. Definitions with an article («qué es una GPU»), identity («quién eres») and «…, quien gana?» keep their model answers with zero operations.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


